jterm: never read FreeRDP's or WinPR's system-wide JSON configuration files.

Besides certificates.json (patch 0001), a system-wide folder is searched for:
  settings-defaults-client.json  any FreeRDP setting, applied as a default: it can turn
                                 certificate checking off or route the connection through a proxy
  the CredSSP configuration      "SspiModule" names a library that is then LOADED for authentication
  the NTLM/Negotiate ones        authentication policy
  remotefx.json                  codec tuning
On Windows that folder is %ProgramData%\<vendor>\<product>\, and every local user may create
folders under %ProgramData%. One user of a shared PC could therefore run code in, or take the
certificate check out of, every other user's RDP helper, the process that holds their password.
Elsewhere the folder is the build machine's install prefix, which is nobody's to rely on.

jterm configures the helper itself and wants no system-wide policy, so both loaders return
"no file" for the system-wide location. Per-user files are untouched (the user's own).

Applies to the FreeRDP version in ../FREERDP_VERSION; regenerate it for a new version rather
than dropping it.

diff --git a/libfreerdp/utils/helpers.c b/libfreerdp/utils/helpers.c
index b92ae82..7998296 100644
--- a/libfreerdp/utils/helpers.c
+++ b/libfreerdp/utils/helpers.c
@@ -300,6 +300,10 @@ char* freerdp_GetConfigFilePath(BOOL system, const char* filename)
 
 WINPR_JSON* freerdp_GetJSONConfigFile(BOOL system, const char* filename)
 {
+	/* jterm: no system-wide configuration file is ever read (see the patch's description). */
+	if (system)
+		return nullptr;
+
 	char* path = freerdp_GetConfigFilePath(system, filename);
 	if (!path)
 		return nullptr;
diff --git a/winpr/libwinpr/path/path.c b/winpr/libwinpr/path/path.c
index 389b362..600f4f8 100644
--- a/winpr/libwinpr/path/path.c
+++ b/winpr/libwinpr/path/path.c
@@ -1421,6 +1421,10 @@ char* winpr_GetConfigFilePathV(BOOL system, const char* filename, ...)
 
 WINPR_JSON* winpr_GetJSONConfigFile(BOOL system, const char* filename)
 {
+	/* jterm: no system-wide configuration file is ever read (see the patch's description). */
+	if (system)
+		return nullptr;
+
 	char* path = winpr_GetConfigFilePath(system, filename);
 	if (!path)
 		return nullptr;
